.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt NVIDIA-UVM-LINUX 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvidia_uvm_linux
.Nd optional Linux ioctl bridge for the NVIDIA unified virtual memory driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "kldload nvidia_uvm_linux"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
module is the optional bridge between the Linuxulator and
.Xr nvidia-uvm 4 .
It offers the Linux request numbers of the UVM interface to third-party
Linux CUDA binaries that run under the Linuxulator.
It is not needed by a native caller: the driver
.Xr nvidia-uvm 4
is the native driver of this system and speaks its own request numbers.
.Pp
The module is loaded by the operator, by hand, after the driver:
.Pp
.Dl kldload nvidia-uvm.ko
.Dl kldload nvidia_uvm_linux.ko
.Pp
Loading it registers a
.Xr linux 4
ioctl handler with the Linuxulator.
The handler answers
.Er ENOIOCTL
for a descriptor that is not one of the driver's two nodes, so that the
Linuxulator can try another handler.
It answers a Linux request number that the driver has no request for as
the driver answers any unknown request:
.Er ENOSYS
on the main node
.Pa /dev/nvidia-uvm
and
.Er EINVAL
on the tools node
.Pa /dev/nvidia-uvm-tools .
.Pp
The handler translates the Linux request number into the request number of
the driver and re-enters the kernel's own ioctl path with it, so that the
per-file state of the driver is found the same way on both paths.
.Pp
The Linuxulator runs a registered ioctl handler with Giant held.
The bridge releases Giant for the duration of each Linux ioctl and relies
on it nowhere.
Giant users such as USB enumeration therefore do not wait behind a long
GPU mapping.
.Pp
The bridge needs the 64-bit Linuxulator: the
.Pa linux64
module on amd64 and the
.Pa linux64elf
module on arm64, and both need
.Pa linux_common .
A 32-bit Linux binary on amd64 is not served.
.Pp
Unloading the bridge unregisters the handler.
The Linuxulator holds its own lock across a handler call and unregistering
the handler takes it exclusively, so the unload waits for a Linux ioctl in
flight to finish.
.Pp
The driver cannot be unloaded while the bridge is loaded: the kernel
refuses to unload a module that another loaded module depends on.
.Pp
This is a clean-room implementation written from a functional
specification, not from NVIDIA's Linux driver.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/nvidia-uvm-tools" -compact
.It Pa /dev/nvidia-uvm
.It Pa /dev/nvidia-uvm-tools
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr linux 4 ,
.Xr nvidia-uvm 4 ,
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr kldunload 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
bridge first appeared in CloudBSD in 2026.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An REVYTECH Inc
.Sh BUGS
The bridge serves the 64-bit Linuxulator only.
A 32-bit Linux binary on amd64 needs the
.Pa linux
module of the 32-bit Linuxulator, which this bridge does not depend on.
